WHAT ASSIGNMENT? — third-party material

MUSIC
- Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart, Requiem in D minor, K. 626, VIII. Lacrimosa (composition: public domain).
  Recording: Bruno Walter, Wiener Philharmoniker, Wiener Staatsopernchor, live at the Salzburg Festival, 26 July 1956.
  Source: https://archive.org/details/MozartRequiemBruno (marked Public Domain Mark 1.0 there; also hosted on Wikimedia Commons as public domain).
  Used: 4.2 s from the "judicandus homo reus" forte, compressed, lightly reverberated, cut dead on the cut to black.
  Note: a 1956 recording is public domain in the EU and under the uploader's marking, but sound-recording terms differ by country
  (in the US, pre-1972 recordings are protected until 2067 at the latest). Check your platform's rules before monetising.
- Opening cue (pizzicato strings, clarinet, bassoon, flute): original, written in mix.py and played with the
  VSCO 2 Community Edition samples (Versilian Studios), CC0 1.0 — https://vis.versilian.com/ (via the Lemo-Opuscar sample packs).

